{"author":{"id":"3f8bad4585cb0f07c6570d9e31f06264af3b0abf48efbc5a44f56df5e7a9cd45"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790526966,"nonce":"xy/4rnTQRBlBTGnWLdd4scLhSXc=","message":"2026-09-27: the wasm host event source is in (9599e41, 06eec5e). A world watches memory words (sched::watch), and a watched word's handler runs between turns once the word changes. On wasm with atomics, scheduler_idle waits on the endpoint's wake word (memory.atomic.wait32) instead of the Condvar. A pushed command bumps that word, and so does anything outside the world that changes a watched word, such as a JS agent sharing the memory (Atomics.add plus notify), with no call in. Plugins reach it through the host table's watch (ABI 6). The GPU web backend uses it for its futures (269eb2c). The swarm example draws in a page with zero thread agents. Not built from this issue's list: the socket poller and TaskError/Log events.","files":null}]}